{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The book Ve-elleh Shemot, composition of Abraham, completed year 4913. Precious as they are." "<b>Ve-elleh.</b> The reason for the vav is because he mentioned at the end of the first book that Joseph saw his sons at thirty years (Genesis 50:22); he mentioned that his brothers, when they descended, were few, and they were fruitful and multiplied. And the word אלה, even with the omission of the he, is the same for masculine and feminine, as it is written כי את כל התועבות האל (Leviticus 18:27), and after it מכל התועבות האלה (ibid. 18:29); לאנשים האל (Genesis 19:8); אלה ילדו להרפה (II Samuel 21:22); מה אעשה לאלה (Genesis 31:43). And likewise the word לז: השונמית הלז (II Kings 4:25); הנער הלז (Zechariah 2:5). And because the word אלה is mil'el, the he was added, like the he of לילה (Genesis 1:5), נחלה מצרים (Numbers 34:5), and it is a masculine noun and plural — שמות — for the tav encompasses the sign of plural for both masculine and feminine, like מקומות and אבות. Also likewise the mem is a sign of both masculine and feminine, like נשים and פלגשים. And there are nouns found with both mem and tav, like נפשים (Ezekiel 13:20), נפשות (ibid. 18), לבבות (I Chronicles 28:9), and also לבבים על לבבהן (Nahum 2:5)." "The he of מצרימה is in place of the word אל, like נלכה דותינה (Genesis 37:17) and ותבא אותי ירושלימה (Ezekiel 8:3)." "<b>Et Ya'akov.</b> With Jacob, like כרת יהוה את אברם (Genesis 15:18)." "<b>Ish u-veito.</b> Those who issue from his loins. And בית nowhere in all Scripture means wife — and behold, the witness: איש וביתו באו, for the wives of the tribes were not in the count of the seventy. And let it not trouble you concerning וכפר בעדו ובעד ביתו (Leviticus 16:6, 11), for its plain sense is his father's house, for there were three who confessed, and Azar the priest, who was his wife by virtue of בעדו, and she is included with him, for the man and his wife are האדם."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:45.968985397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}